      "title": "Hybrid quantum computer reproduces a classic quantum effect",
      "summary": "Oxford physicists used a hybrid machine of qubits and quantum oscillators to simulate the Aharonov–Bohm effect, where a particle picks up a measurable phase going around a magnetic flux it never touches. It shows that mixing two kinds of quantum parts can model physics that is hard for ordinary computers. It remains a lab simulation, and the machines are still far from routine scientific use.",
